## 📊 Dataset

This project uses the **CHB-MIT Scalp EEG Database**, a widely used, clinically validated dataset for epilepsy research, published by **John Guttag (MIT)** and hosted on **PhysioNet**.

### Dataset Overview
- EEG recordings from **22 pediatric subjects** with intractable epilepsy
- Collected at **Children’s Hospital Boston**
- Subjects monitored for several days following withdrawal of anti-seizure medication
- **182 expert-annotated seizures** with precise onset and offset times
- Continuous scalp EEG recordings sampled at **256 Hz**
- Electrode placement follows the **International 10–20 system**

### Data Structure
- Recordings are organized into **23 cases** (`chb01`, `chb02`, …)
- Each case contains **9–42 EDF files** from a single subject
- Files are typically **1 hour long** (some are 2–4 hours)
- Seizure intervals are provided via accompanying **`.edf.seizures` annotation files**
- Files listed in `RECORDS-WITH-SEIZURES` contain one or more seizures

### Signal Characteristics
- 16-bit resolution EEG signals
- Most recordings contain **23 EEG channels**
- Additional signals (e.g., ECG, VNS) are present in select cases
- All protected health information (PHI) has been removed or anonymized

### Dataset Access
The dataset is publicly available under the **Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0** and can be accessed from:

https://physionet.org/content/chbmit/1.0.0/

Access requires agreeing to PhysioNet’s data usage terms.

